![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

The `_stash_hisparse_spec_info` helper method is duplicated 5 times in `BatchResultProcessor`. Please remove the redundant definitions and keep only one.

```suggestion
    def _stash_hisparse_spec_info(
        self, batch: ScheduleBatch, batch_index: int, req: Req
    ) -> None:
        if not self.server_args.enable_hisparse or batch.spec_info is None:
            return
        if not hasattr(batch.spec_info, "slice_single"):
            raise RuntimeError(
                "HiSparse cannot stash speculative state for "
                f"{type(batch.spec_info).__name__}"
            )
        req.hisparse_spec_info = batch.spec_info.slice_single(batch_index)
```

![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

If `device_slots.numel() < compressed.numel()`, the mapping is silently skipped, which can lead to silent correctness issues or undefined behavior. Please raise a `RuntimeError` to fail fast and prevent silent failures.

```suggestion
        if compressed.numel() > 0:
            if device_slots.numel() < compressed.numel():
                raise RuntimeError(
                    f"HiSparse: device_slots size ({device_slots.numel()}) is less than "
                    f"required compressed indices ({compressed.numel()})."
                )
            self.full_to_hisparse_device_index_mapping[compressed] = (
                device_slots[:compressed.numel()].to(torch.int64)
            )
```

